# The root .gitattributes routes every *.png/*.jpg in the repo through Git
# LFS, which is right for Assets/ textures but wrong here: GitHub Pages'
# Actions-based deploy does a plain `actions/checkout` with no LFS smudging,
# so an LFS-tracked image under site/ would ship as its pointer stub instead
# of the actual bytes — a broken <img> on the live page. These two
# screenshots are a few hundred KB total; there's no reason to pull LFS
# (and its bandwidth quota) into a static landing page. Un-set the filter and
# treat them as ordinary binary blobs.
*.png -filter -diff -merge -text
*.jpg -filter -diff -merge -text
